;; The appliance on a Radxa Rock 5B.
;;
;; RK3588: four A76 and four A55, up to 32GB, NVMe on M.2, and the fastest
;; board here by some distance. Imported from Buildroot's own rock5b_defconfig
;; rather than assembled by hand, so the bootloader chain - ATF v2.12 for
;; rk3588, U-Boot with the rkbin DDR blob, the idbloader layout - is the one
;; the release ships and was proven to round-trip.
;;
;; The rootfs is larger than the board profile's 250M. An earlier hand-built
;; attempt at this image failed at the last step, after twenty-eight minutes,
;; because the RK3588's kernel modules do not fit a small rootfs; a size is a
;; value rather than a minimum, so an image that needs more says so here.

(image rock5b-bringup
  (compose
    image:rock5b
    feature:dev-ssh
    feature:modbus
    feature:fieldbus-test)

  (override
    (value buildroot:BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE "512M"))

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
